        "raw": "Based on my expeience, most of the villains can be beaten by the same general strategy and don't need their own guide.\r\n\r\nBring a lot of damage (this can include support that increases damage, but preferably not very many).  If the villain has any problematic ongoings (a lot don't), bring some heroes that destroy them (not every hero, but more than 1), and the same goes for the environment.  Remove/attack/otherwise get rid of cards that seem at least moderately threatening and do damage to the villain as a secondary goal.  It doesn't work for everything, but I've beaten every villain and played countless games, and believe it should be effective on about 2/3 of them without much other strategy.\r\n\r\nA lot of villains cetainly need more thought, and I have used many tips and tricks found on on these forums.  They aren't always in guides, but I just do a search for the villain name or a particular card.  That works pretty well.  There are a lot of useful discussions on these forums.",
